  "preferred_feature": "Emphysema on imaging",
  "rationale": "Emphysema on imaging has stronger validation-based evidence for treatment-benefit heterogeneity. Its univariable R-learner validation R-loss gains were positive in 3 of 3 analyses (0.004, 0.006, 0.003), and causal-forest permutation R-loss increases were positive in 3 of 3 analyses (0.003, 0.004, 0.002), indicating consistent improvement in predicting differences in treatment effect over a constant effect. It also had nonzero penalized treatment interactions in 3 of 3 analyses. By contrast, serum creatinine had R-learner gains that were negative or zero in all three analyses, positive causal-forest permutation increases in only 1 of 3 analyses, and nonzero penalized interactions in only 1 of 3 analyses. Although serum creatinine was consistently selected as an outcome main effect, that mainly indicates prognostic value rather than reliable treatment-effect modification. Nominal interaction p-values were broadly similar for the two variables and lack multiplicity-adjusted q-values, so they do not overturn the clearer validation evidence for emphysema. The practical magnitude of the gain remains uncertain because baseline losses and uncertainty estimates are not provided, but the direction and consistency favor emphysema."
